======================================================================
  Forest Link Protocol — Raspberry Pi Gateway Deployment
======================================================================

  Deploys three services on a Raspberry Pi to bridge ESP32 mesh
  nodes to the cloud:

    1. Mosquitto        MQTT broker              TCP 1883
    2. MQTT-SN Gateway  UDP-to-MQTT translator   UDP 1885 -> TCP 1883
    3. FLP MQTT Admin   File transfer manager    connects to localhost:1883

  ESP32 nodes speak MQTT-SN over UDP. The gateway translates that
  into standard MQTT for the broker. The admin subscribes to the
  broker and handles file reassembly with Selective Repeat ARQ.


REQUIREMENTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  - Raspberry Pi 3B+ or newer (tested on Pi 4, Pi 5)
  - Raspberry Pi OS (Bookworm) or Ubuntu 22.04+
  - Internet access (for initial package install)
  - Same WiFi network as the ESP32 gateway nodes


QUICK START
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. Copy this directory to the Pi (scp, USB, git clone, etc.)

  2. Run the installer:

       sudo bash deploy.sh --install

     This will:
       - Install and configure Mosquitto
       - Clone and build the Eclipse Paho MQTT-SN gateway
       - Create a Python venv and install pip dependencies
       - Register all three as systemd services (auto-start on boot)

  3. Verify everything is running:

       bash deploy.sh --status


COMMANDS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  sudo bash deploy.sh --install      Full install (packages + services)
  sudo bash deploy.sh --start        Start all services
  sudo bash deploy.sh --stop         Stop all services
       bash deploy.sh --status       Show service status
  sudo bash deploy.sh --uninstall    Remove all services and configs


MANAGING SERVICES INDIVIDUALLY
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  sudo systemctl start   mosquitto
  sudo systemctl stop    mosquitto
  sudo systemctl restart mosquitto
  sudo systemctl status  mosquitto

  sudo systemctl start   mqtt-sn-gateway
  sudo systemctl stop    mqtt-sn-gateway
  sudo systemctl restart mqtt-sn-gateway
  sudo systemctl status  mqtt-sn-gateway

  sudo systemctl start   flp-mqtt-admin
  sudo systemctl stop    flp-mqtt-admin
  sudo systemctl restart flp-mqtt-admin
  sudo systemctl status  flp-mqtt-admin


VIEWING LOGS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Follow logs in real time (Ctrl+C to stop):

    journalctl -u mosquitto -f
    journalctl -u mqtt-sn-gateway -f
    journalctl -u flp-mqtt-admin -f

  Last 50 lines of a service:

    journalctl -u flp-mqtt-admin -n 50


RUNNING THE ADMIN MANUALLY (without systemd)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  If you prefer to run the MQTT admin in the foreground for
  debugging, stop the service first and run it directly:

    sudo systemctl stop flp-mqtt-admin
    cd cloud-admin
    .venv/bin/python3 mqtt_admin.py --broker localhost --port 1883

  Options:

    -b, --broker HOST    MQTT broker hostname  (default: localhost)
    -p, --port   PORT    MQTT broker port      (default: 1883)

  Press Ctrl+C to stop. A session summary is printed on exit.


OUTPUT FILES
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Received files are saved to:

    cloud-admin/received_files/<filename>

  The directory is created automatically on first transfer.


NETWORK TOPOLOGY
----------------------------------------------------------------------

    ESP32 nodes                  Raspberry Pi
  +-----------+               +-----------------------------+
  | MQTT-SN   |  UDP :1885    | MQTT-SN   |    | Mosquitto |
  | Client    | ------------> | Gateway   | -> | Broker    |
  +-----------+               +-----------+    | TCP :1883 |
                                               +-----+-----+
                                                     |
                                               +-----+-----+
                                               | FLP MQTT  |
                                               | Admin     |
                                               +-----------+
                                                     |
                                               received_files/


PORTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Port    Proto   Service             Direction
  ----    -----   -------             ---------
  1883    TCP     Mosquitto           Inbound (LAN)
  1885    UDP     MQTT-SN Gateway     Inbound (LAN)

  Make sure your firewall allows these ports if enabled:

    sudo ufw allow 1883/tcp
    sudo ufw allow 1885/udp


TROUBLESHOOTING
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Service won't start
    Check logs:  journalctl -u <service-name> -n 30
    Verify Mosquitto is running first — the gateway depends on it.

  Nodes can't connect
    Confirm the Pi and ESP32 nodes are on the same network.
    Test with:  mosquitto_sub -t "flp/#" -v
    (Should show messages when nodes publish.)

  Build fails for MQTT-SN gateway
    Ensure cmake, g++, and libssl-dev are installed:
      sudo apt-get install cmake g++ libssl-dev

  Python import errors
    Re-create the venv:
      rm -rf .venv
      python3 -m venv .venv
      .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt

